# Two classes with one local name, each with its own property (#485). `a:` holds the most
# classes, so it is the home namespace and a:Cat keeps the plain name.
@prefix a: <http://example.org/a#> .
@prefix b: <http://example.org/b#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/zoo> a owl:Ontology .

a:Cat a owl:Class .
a:Dog a owl:Class .
b:Cat a owl:Class .

a:purrs a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain a:Cat ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean .
b:meows a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain b:Cat ; rdfs:range xsd:boolean .
